        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{41}}{4}$",
          "worked": "Rearrange to $2x^2+3x-4=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{3^2-4(2)(-4)}}{2(2)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{41}}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-f3075-p38-practice-slot-1-upper-slot-1-upper-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$-2x^2+6x+1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{3\\pm\\sqrt{11}}{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-6\\pm\\sqrt{6^2-4(-2)(1)}}{2(-2)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-6\\pm\\sqrt{44}}{-4}\\\\x&=\\frac{-6\\pm2\\sqrt{11}}{-4}\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\mp\\sqrt{11}}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nBoth signs are included, so $x=\\dfrac{3\\pm\\sqrt{11}}{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
